cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ertkit in your work, please cite it as below, together with the methods it implements."
title: "ertkit: verified VES and 2.5-D ERT inversion for groundwater exploration"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tiamiyu
    given-names: "Abd'gafar Tunde"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1641-7196"
    affiliation: "School of Mathematics, Jilin University"
# A version and a Zenodo DOI are added with release 0.1.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/abdgafartunde/ertkit"
url: "https://abdgafartunde.github.io/ertkit/"
abstract: >-
  ertkit inverts vertical electrical sounding (VES) and 2.5-D electrical
  resistivity tomography (ERT) data for groundwater exploration. Each result
  comes with a data error model and a fit to the noise level, sensitivity and
  depth of investigation, and parameter uncertainty, including the range of
  equivalent models for VES.
keywords:
  - electrical resistivity tomography
  - vertical electrical sounding
  - groundwater
  - inverse problems
  - uncertainty quantification
